WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.230
<b>Host
Sakai Masato
<i>No Longer Human</i> was published in June 1948.</b>

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:04.600
Right after that, on June 16, came shocking news.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.110
<b>June 16,
1948</b>

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.570
Right after that, on June 16, came shocking news.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:08.860
<b>June 16,
1948</b>

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:09.070
Asahi Shimbun
Dated 1947.06.16

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.400
Dazai Osamu had committed suicide.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.320
He died at the age of 38.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.240
His suicide note said: "I can't write anymore".

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.490
He committed suicide right after it was published.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.750
And judging by its contents, one could think of
<i>No Longer Human</i> as Dazai Osamu's autobiographical work.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.920
<b>Autobiographical Work
Dazai Osamu's</b>

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.330
<b>Dazai Osamu's
Autobiographical Work</b>

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:26.920
The main character of <i>No Longer Human</i>, Oba Yozo, and Dazai certainly have a lot in common.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.130
<b>Oba Yozo</b>

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.010
<b>Dazai Osamu
Oba Yozo</b>

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.430
Upbringing, women, drugs, alcohol, suicide.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.720
A vestigial photo can support this.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.970
<b>A
photo</b>

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:39.300
<b>Photo credit:
Museum of Modern Japanese Literature</b>

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.270
A photo of Dazai's family taken when he was young.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:42.310
<b>Dazai Osamu</b>

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.850
He has a remarkably big smile on his face.
<b>Photo credit:
Museum of Modern Japanese Literature
Dazai Osamu</b>

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.360
His expression doesn't blend in with the rest of the family.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.860
He's the only one smiling.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:54.070
One can see that behind this smile hides suffering.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.030
The
masterpieces
are blue
The masterpieces are blue.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.950
And now, here's the second episode of <i>No Longer Human</i>.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.500
Ever since I was a child,

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.880
I've been kissing people's asses.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.110
All right, Yozo!

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.360
Nice smile!

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:39.030
But I've been afraid of them.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.420
So I decided to play the clown.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:56.220
That was my last attempt to attract humans.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:17.990
Playing the clown created a faint link between humans and myself.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:25.080
On the surface, I was constantly putting on a smile.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.460
But on the inside, I was desperate and sweating.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.630
That was on purpose.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.830
He found out I was playing the clown.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.750
He's a dangerous guy.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.100
Hey, lemme walk under your umbrella for part of the way.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:26.970
Why would I?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.970
I don't wanna catch the stupid.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:28.720
Let's go!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.350
Yeah.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:34.610
Hey!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.530
You don't have an umbrella?

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.490
My house isn't far. Come with me.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.560
My ears hurt!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.070
Your ears are running really bad.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.780
The rain must have soaked in.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.070
I'll clean them out for you.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.170
You're kind.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.830
Girls must fall for you.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.670
We're friends.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:45.550
So don't speak ill of me to other people.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.050
Monster.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:49.890
A monster?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.810
What?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.850
Your true form.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.140
Mine?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:54.890
Yep.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.560
Wow.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.940
People have called me cute, cool, interesting, et cetera.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.400
But I've never been called a monster.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:23.670
You can see the truth?

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:24.920
Yeah.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.100
I'm not human.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.020
That's right.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.230
Therefore, I'm a monster!

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.140
Oh, you've come to your senses.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.310
Good.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.810
Do you know who you are?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.060
A monster...

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.520
I'm Oba Yozo.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.690
He's awake!

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.530
Yozo!

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.160
You did it!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.960
That woman died.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.710
Died?

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.920
You were the only one who survived.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:57.520
Your father instructed me to look after you from now on.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.140
Why?

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:03.150
You are a hindrance to his
position as a congressman.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:07.780
He said he would by all means cut off any parent-child relationships with you.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.790
The family of the deceased will be taken care of with money.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.410
"Family of the deceased"?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.250
"Taken care of"?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.630
What was her name?

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:28.260
I must meet with her family.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.270
The military's hidden agenda on the continent...

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:50.940
It's obvious that the Japanese government is aiming to expand onto the continent to overcome the recession!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:56.620
The readers should know that a deserter from the Japanese Army caused Zhang Zoulin's train to explode last year—

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.540
Who's interested in articles like that?

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.410
Put that aside.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.710
This man is about to leave the hospital.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:06.000
Interview this guy.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.710
A man who committed a double suicide with a woman and survived.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.970
It's possible that it was a murder, not an accident!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.680
He pretended to go along with the
double suicide then killed her on purpose!

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:20.270
Why would he do that?

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.730
Beats me.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.520
If that's true,

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.360
then this guy is a disgrace to men.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.320
Wives love articles like those.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:31.860
He's at the Kamakura hospital.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.110
Kamakura... You want me to go now?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.570
Yeah, hurry up.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:36.820
I'll arrange a meeting for you.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.040
Maybe he likes middle-aged women.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.330
If a sexy lady like you comes,

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.960
he might spill the beans.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:50.550
I'm so very sorry, but my child is waiting for me.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.340
I'm done for today.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.090
This is why women are useless!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.090
I'm not renewing your contract.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.100
Tagosuke!

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.180
You go!

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.390
Thanks as usual.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.380
Hey you!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.960
It's dangerous!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.670
I'm sorry.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.930
I'm home, Shigeko!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.180
I'll cook dinner now.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.310
What were you drawing?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.350
Daddy.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.780
Daddy's not with us anymore.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.410
But he's always watching you from above.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.660
I'm hungry.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.130
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.000
I'll cook some sweet bread for you.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.480
Mom, it hurts.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.570
Sorry.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:54.750
Shortly after meeting her,
you buried your face in her skirt?

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:55.750
Yes.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.380
How did it feel?

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.050
How...

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.470
Well.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.180
It smelled good.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:08.060
What?

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.560
A smell I'd never smelled before.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.520
It was arousing.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.820
I felt like I could die anytime.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.610
Then I wanted to commit a double suicide.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.870
Are you all right?

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:31.330
No way!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.710
He coughed up bloody phlegm!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:34.960
He has tuberculosis.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:41.220
I have to go report to my superior now.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.630
What about the investigation?

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.550
Forget about it.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:47.930
It's over.

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.240
It's like I said!

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.240
Detectives are a joke.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.000
Hey, what are you doing?

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.510
Now listen to my request.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.260
It's a special exclusive interview!

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.720
Thanks a lot.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.680
No, no!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.890
Pay the money you promised me first.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.680
Oh, sorry about that.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.190
Thanks!

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.060
Isn't it a good picture? He looks so arrogant.

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:40.280
So did he really kill her?

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.860
But anyway, isn't he a good-looking man?

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.280
Women must fall for him.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.370
Hey, Shizuko, would you fall for him?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.910
Isn't he still a boy?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.790
No use asking the iron lady.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.670
So what about this guy's interview?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.420
What was his explanation?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.090
"I failed to commit a double suicide."

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.430
"There's no way I would kill her."

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.930
No one would call himself a murderer, right?

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.560
What about the woman's family?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.100
They must have been paid off.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.770
They refused to say anything.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.690
Even though their daughter got killed?

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:26.200
Mr. Oba is extremely angry that your photo got published in a magazine.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:28.780
He says it affects his life as a congressman.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.200
Geez.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.700
You take your eyes off this guy for one second and he gets his picture taken.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:41.250
Hey, want me to keep looking after you?

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:45.010
He's obviously getting money from your father.

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.880
If I were the one getting it...

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.760
I don't want to rely on you.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.560
So that's how it is.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.520
Hey, wait!

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.060
Did you forget?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.610
I'm the one who was looking after him until now.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.820
See you later!

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:12.410
As a final favor, I'll try to stay away from the system. You'd better appreciate it.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.580
Driver, let's go.

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:24.500
Your father asked me to observe you so you don't try to commit suicide again.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.590
I've withdrawn you from school.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.140
Please put up with this inconvenience.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.780
This is your room.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.530
You mustn't leave it.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:56.870
What am I supposed to do in here if I'm not allowed to leave?

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.250
Please read magazines or something.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.420
I have work to do.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.680
I want to die.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:20.350
But it'd be stupid to drown myself again.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.100
There's a picture of a monster.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.810
A picture of a monster?

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.480
It's Van Gogh's self-portrait.

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.440
It's a picture of a monster.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.490
This is a picture of a monster?

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.990
Van Gogh is a monster?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.200
I never thought so.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.120
Okay.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.670
I'll draw a picture of a monster too!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:43.370
That's it.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.620
I'll draw pictures of monsters.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.170
The real me!

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:52.920
Yesterday, the Chicago market was shut down.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:56.220
The chaos of the world economy probably isn't going to end.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:18:01.180
Even in our country, many companies will probably go bankrupt.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.280
This is me!

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:20.450
If I'm reborn...

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.040
If I'm reborn...

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.590
I'd like to live more like a human.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.440
No.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.860
A monster can't live among humans.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:25.680
From now on, I'll live more like a human.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.830
I'd like to get the manuscripts.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.750
I'm fixing up the cuts.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.710
Wait a minute, please.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.340
Please come in!

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:02.090
What are you doing here?

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:14.980
Uh...

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:17.820
Don't mind him.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.360
Would a person who escaped death drink tea?

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:23.780
Oh, about that.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.120
See, this guy committed a
double suicide with a woman.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.580
And came home alone.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:34.330
I'm a pure-hearted artist, so I know him very well.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:39.000
I can't abandon artists who were
crushed by the weight of this era.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.590
Is he the guy from Kamakura...?

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.380
Exactly!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.930
You know of him?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:50.770
He said he wouldn't rely on me, but he came here...

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.640
Maybe he doesn't have any other friends.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:05.610
Uh...

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.570
Shouldn't we go check on him?

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:08.780
Why?

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.660
Somehow,

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.750
he just looked so lost.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:16.210
That's his trick.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:17.790
Don't be fooled.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.510
It's just as Horiki said.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.340
I said I wanted to live "like a human", but I can't do anything by myself.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.850
That's who I am.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:37.560
You have nowhere to stay?

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:43.280
If you'd like, you can come to my place.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.610
But our living conditions aren't that great.

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:50.240
Hope you don't mind.

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.410
Hooray!

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:59.290
Then let's go.

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.000
Okay.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:30.090
Society
Episode Three
Next Time
No Longer Human
